@* "Open this repository on GitHub in a new tab" icon link.

   The same <a><RadzenIcon Icon="open_in_new"/></a> snippet with the same target=_blank /
   title / aria-label trio lived on the Repositories grid row and on the RepositoryDetail hero
   for the only purpose of telling the user "yes, this is the same GitHub URL the rest of the
   app uses, click here". Two copies of the markup had already drifted: the grid's was wrapped
   in `<span @onclick:stopPropagation="true">` so the row-click handler would not fire, the
   detail page's was not (it sits next to the title so there is no row-click). Centralising
   the markup deletes that drift risk and lets the click-in-row-grid pattern be a single
   parameter on this component. *@

@using Radzen
@using Radzen.Blazor

@* `StopRowClickPropagation`: true when the link sits inside a row that handles its own click
   (the repositories grid) — the click on the link must not bubble into the row handler. False
   on the detail page where the link sits in the hero beside a heading and there is no row. *@
<span @onclick:stopPropagation="@StopRowClickPropagation">
    <a href="@Url"
       target="_blank"
       rel="noopener noreferrer"
       title="@Title"
       aria-label="@Title"
       class="github-link @($"github-link--{Size.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()}")">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="open_in_new" class="github-link__icon" />
    </a>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>Absolute GitHub URL — typically <c>https://github.com/{owner}/{name}</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Url { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Accessible label and hover title; should describe what opens, e.g. <c>Open foo/bar on GitHub in a new tab</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>True on the grid row — see StopRowClickPropagation comment.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool StopRowClickPropagation { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Compact for table rows, Medium for heroes.</summary>
    [Parameter] public LinkSize Size { get; set; } = LinkSize.Compact;

    /// <summary>Size hint for the link — inline enum so callers don't need a separate using.</summary>
    public enum LinkSize { Compact, Medium }
}